## Summary
Brazil's General Data Protection Law (LGPD), enacted in 2018 and set to take effect in February 2020, is a data protection regulation often compared to the European Union's GDPR. This article provides an overview of the LGPD, highlighting its key features, implementation timeline, and how it differs from or resembles the GDPR.

## Key Points
- Brazil passed the LGPD (Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados) in 2018.
- The LGPD will come into effect in February 2020.
- The LGPD is modeled after the GDPR, with specific differences and similarities in data protection requirements.


